From 0fa6baf7093b9c7e3c7b4dd05b017c657cd3eb41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:14:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 203/204] Show the Chrome Web Store at phone width

Patch 0024 sent the Chrome Web Store as a desktop site by storing a
desktop-site exception for it. The exception was written for the
store's registrable domain, google.com, so Search, Gmail, Maps and every
other Google site also opened in desktop mode on phones.

The store only needs the desktop user agent. With a mobile one it swaps
"Add to Chrome" for "Add to Desktop", which sends the extension to a
signed-in desktop Chrome instead of installing it. Its pages fit any
width as long as their viewport tag is honoured, and desktop mode
normally turns that tag off.

chromewebstore.google.com now gets the desktop user agent from code, for
navigations the browser starts and ones the page starts, and keeps its
viewport tag, so the store fits the phone and its install button works.
A desktop-site setting the user makes for the store still wins.

On first launch the google.com exception from earlier versions is
removed, once.
